          "kind": "informational",
          "level": "none",
          "guid": "mrwoi29dgc70mf94",
          "message": {
            "text": "Drive-spawned entries are spared by \"Disconnect all\" for the same reason worker entries are: SIGTERMing one would yank the MCP server out from under an in-flight one-shot play run (the \"never kill a worker mid-ticket\" principle). They are also excluded from `pickLeader`'s main preference so a `codex exec` run's temporary connection can never capture the trigger-routing leadership from a real interactive session.\n",
            "markdown": "Drive-spawned entries are spared by \"Disconnect all\" for the same reason worker entries are: SIGTERMing one would yank the MCP server out from under an in-flight one-shot play run (the \"never kill a worker mid-ticket\" principle). They are also excluded from `pickLeader`'s main preference so a `codex exec` run's temporary connection can never capture the trigger-routing leadership from a real interactive session.\n"
          },
          "locations": [
            {
              "physicalLocation": {
                "artifactLocation": {
                  "uri": "src/channelRegistry.ts"
                },
                "region": {
                  "startLine": 139,
                  "endLine": 146,
                  "snippet": {
                    "text": "\n/** Pure — the MAIN connections among `entries`: not a distributed worker's\n *  (`worktree` set, HS-9038) and not a drive-spawned one-shot run's (`drive`\n *  set, HS-9380). These are the only entries the multi-connection warning\n *  counts and the \"Disconnect all\" cleanup tears down. */\nexport function mainConnections(entries: ChannelInfo[]): ChannelInfo[] {\n  return entries.filter(e => e.worktree == null && e.drive !== true);\n}"
                  }
                }
              }
            }
          ],
          "properties": {
            "tags": [
              "rationale"
            ]
          },
